Experimental immutable context/key front end

Original Go additions: SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0.

This test-only package adapts the context tree, joining isolation labels,
ancestor-first interception and per-consumer availability semantics of
@deepseek-ai/cordis 4.1.0, as modified and published by DeepSeek Harness.
Source-content pin: fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159
https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/tree/fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159
Reference files: vendor/cordis/src/context.ts and service.ts (the preserved
oracle copies are test/differential/oracle/vendor/cordis/src/context.ts and
service.ts). Source package pin: @deepseek-ai/cordis 4.1.0, archive SHA-256
3b0099a6aa9b0b52c3e199042acf6f1ae195c5690f7de11aa61171bca7752eca.

Go adaptations/additions include typed name+major keys, exact-type collision
validation, registered entry-value identity, explicit binding data, immutable
provision snapshots, declared dependencies, typed scope values and explicit
audiences. They are experimental metadata, not the selected kernel, a mounted
runtime or a claim of full S0 acceptance. Lifecycle/ACTIVE publication, effect
ownership, leases, epochs, hooks and both runtime integrations remain separate.
No package name or public API here selects the eventual kernel SDK layout.

